   "fieldname": "replacement_help",
   "fieldtype": "HTML",
   "label": "Replacement Help",
   "options": "<div class=\"small\" style=\"border:1px solid var(--border-color);border-radius:6px;padding:8px 10px\"><b>How many replacement donors?</b> One donor gives one bag (about 450 ml) = 1 unit. Units are counted in bags, not millilitres. One split bag gives 1 Red Cells + 1 FFP + 1 Platelets, so one donor covers one unit of each.<table class=\"table table-bordered table-sm\" style=\"margin:6px 0\"><tr><th>Patient needs</th><th>Donors (1 per unit)</th></tr><tr><td>2 Whole Blood</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>2 Red Cells</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>2 Red Cells + 2 FFP</td><td>2 (same bags are split)</td></tr><tr><td>1 Whole Blood + 1 Red Cells</td><td>2 (each needs its own bag)</td></tr><tr><td>4 Platelets</td><td>4</td></tr></table>The number is filled for you from Settings &gt; Replacement Donors per Unit. Change it if the doctor or policy asks for more (e.g. 2 per unit to rebuild stock). Relatives do not need the patient&#39;s blood group: their blood restocks the bank.</div>"
